page('Ablations and per tier findings',head('7 Ablations'),fig('06_paired_and_ablations','Figure 4  Paired effects. Core and exploratory comparisons have different testing roles.'),para('JointSLA versus its shortest-queue routing ablation is −2.10 percentage points, with interval [−4.84, +0.73] and raw exploratory p = 0.158844. The interval crosses zero and does not establish a separate routing benefit. JointSLA versus reactive scaling with the Joint router is −11.05 points, with interval [−13.73, −8.30] and raw exploratory p = 3.147870e−07, consistent with a scaling/headroom contribution.'),para('Rule replacement changes feedback and realized replica trajectories. These arms cannot uniquely decompose the gain. Joint scaler/shortest queue uses 112.84 target replica-seconds compared with JointSLA’s 103.45, while reactive/Joint router uses 65.44. These are exploratory observations.'),table(['Policy','Gold failures %','Silver failures %','Bronze failures %'],tierrows[:4]),para('JointSLA Gold fails 10,201 of 12,810 requests, or 79.63%, versus 96.49% for reactive. Silver and Bronze fail at 35.94% and 34.06%. FIFO admission, differing deadlines and shared resources prevent interpreting this as robust priority-tier protection.')),
